		<li id="LI_FF0D8BA2B5EF4569B5E21DE6C80C1460"><b>Configuration of Downstream Source Decoder:</b> 
		  <p> 
			 <ph>Nova Lake</ph> platform removes the OPI controller connecting SOC-North &lt;-&gt; SOC- South and connects them directly via PSF hierarchy. IO range and MMIO range decoding which was handled by DMI in PCH is now moved to IOC. Previously BIOS was programming DMI registers through P2SB mechanism in PCH. Decode related registers are now part of Device0 Configuration space in IOC. 
			 <note id="GUID-002513D0-402E-42CB-88B3-691DDCA48AE8">BIOS must program these registers and lock them down as part of boot flow. 
			 </note> 
		  </p> 
